cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GottLUX in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GottLUX: an open-source event-based sensor toolkit"
abstract: >-
  An open-source toolkit that removes the barrier to working with event-based (neuromorphic)
  cameras: a vendor-free Prophesee .raw decoder with sub-second sampled preview of
  multi-gigabyte recordings, HDF5 interchange in both directions, an interactive instrument
  (live viewer, 3-D space-time explorer, event-rate tower, flutter workbench), a
  temporal-frequency detection and tracking engine, de-rotation and fusion for spinning and
  dual-sensor payloads, EBS-acoustic fusion, a clip-and-canvas video editor, one-command
  export of analyses as standalone MATLAB and Python scripts, and reproducible
  provenance-stamped results.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gott
    given-names: Simon
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-29"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sijon8/GottLUX"
keywords:
  - event-based sensor
  - event camera
  - neuromorphic
  - event-based vision
  - Prophesee
  - frequency analysis
  - tracking
  - visualization
  - video editing
  - open source
